00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.530
Okay, Chris, it's now or never.

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:34.450
Remember what Arrow taught you.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.500
What do you think, Martino?

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.610
Beautiful, aren't they?

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:44.960
Not again, sleep.

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.870
Ah! They are gone!

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:48.720
Where are my earrings?

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.870
Got you, little Tarsars.

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:52.910
What did you do?

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.750
Where are my earrings?

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:56.260
I don't know.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.640
What? What is he saying?

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:00.000
Pose him, Dobby.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:12.250
I don't know where they went.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.350
It happens, you know?

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.990
I mean, I misplace things all the time.

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:18.850
I have it one minute, then I do something else, and boom, it's gone.

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:23.330
I usually find it in my backpack, or maybe my sock, or my boot, or my flipper, but--

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.290
Enough!

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:30.000
If any more of my precious fashions disappear, it's your fault.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.900
- Where's my baby leopard shawl?

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:36.600
- You know, my brother, now he's pretty organized.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.960
He might be able to help you keep track of stuff.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.640
Just sayin'.

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:42.480
- Danita.

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:49.480
- Tell me where my animals are.

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:52.210
- We'll need that baby pangolin back too, Danita.

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:02.980
You don't give me back my animals.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:04.380
I'm not giving back your brother.

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:11.180
Back off, Dobby-o!

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:15.590
I'm getting the post-beat deactivation ball!

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:18.660
Get him!

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:24.060
Got you covered, bro.

00:22:28.930 --> 00:22:29.550
Got it!

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:30.000
Martin!

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:50.550
behind you. Look out!

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:09.440
Yeah, the baby animals are free. Now, let's get you back to where you belong. Living free and in the wild.

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:13.610
You can keep your little

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:19.050
animal jewels. They weren't that precious anyway. Let's go, Domio.

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:29.440
There you go, buddy. Back to mama. Well, that's all of them. It's a creature mission accomplished.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.960
we learned all about an amazing fish

00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:34.400
with a very unique creature power.

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:36.980
- And I became a master at archer fishery.

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:44.160
And I finally got the suction arrow off.

00:23:48.770 --> 00:23:51.730
- So the archer fish is an ordinary little fish

00:23:51.730 --> 00:23:54.170
with an extraordinary creature power.

00:23:54.170 --> 00:23:57.210
And now it's time for a detailed breakdown

00:23:57.210 --> 00:23:59.540
of the archer fish power in action.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:07.560
An archerfish swims close to the water's surface, scanning above, looking for prey.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:13.260
They look at the branches hanging over the water, like that one, where insects might be.

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:15.970
And they're really good at spotting movement.

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:19.210
An archerfish takes time to aim, fire!

00:24:19.210 --> 00:24:25.730
And the glob of water goes flying right to the target and hits in a powerful glob.

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:30.000
An archerfish is really good at predicting where that insect he hits is going to

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:35.770
land so he can get there and gobble it up before any other archerfish can.

00:24:35.770 --> 00:24:39.230
An archerfish isn't born with perfect aim.

00:24:39.230 --> 00:24:41.650
That only comes with practice.

00:24:41.650 --> 00:24:43.100
And observation.

00:24:43.100 --> 00:24:48.010
Because young archerfish watch experienced archerfish spitting the globs of water at

00:24:48.010 --> 00:24:48.950
insects.

00:24:48.950 --> 00:24:51.590
Whoa!

00:24:51.590 --> 00:24:53.270
That happened so fast.

00:24:53.270 --> 00:24:54.530
We gotta slow it down.

00:24:54.530 --> 00:24:57.870
We gotta see it in slow motion.

00:24:57.870 --> 00:25:00.000
He shoots and bam!

00:25:00.250 --> 00:25:03.010
The insect is knocked into the water below.

00:25:03.010 --> 00:25:08.620
What a creature power.

00:25:08.620 --> 00:25:15.800
Whoa, them, perfect aim for the archer fish.

00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:18.780
All right, it's time for a Wild Kratz experiment.

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:20.500
All right, we're trying to find out.

00:25:20.500 --> 00:25:23.460
From how far away can an archer fish shoot

00:25:23.460 --> 00:25:25.500
and hit a target with accuracy?

00:25:25.500 --> 00:25:28.870
All right, let's try it way up here.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.690
- Okay, let's see, this one's getting ready to go.

00:25:32.690 --> 00:25:35.300
Ready to shoot, eyeing it.

00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:37.880
- Oh, yes!

00:25:37.880 --> 00:25:39.160
- That was great!

00:25:39.160 --> 00:25:41.470
That was a good four or five feet.

00:25:41.470 --> 00:25:43.610
- An archerfish can hit his target

00:25:43.610 --> 00:25:45.790
from as far as nine feet away.

00:25:45.790 --> 00:25:48.650
- All right, feeding time and archery practice

00:25:48.650 --> 00:25:49.690
look like they're over.

00:25:49.690 --> 00:25:51.190
'Til next time they're hungry.

00:25:51.190 --> 00:25:54.230
And then the amazing archerfish will once again

00:25:54.230 --> 00:25:56.490
let those water arrows fly.

00:25:56.490 --> 00:25:57.930
- Keep on creature adventuring.

00:25:57.930 --> 00:25:59.830
We'll see you on the Creature Trail.

00:26:17.920 --> 00:26:23.290
about cool animals and collect your own Wild Kratz creature powers go to the

00:26:23.290 --> 00:26:26.950
Wild Kratz website at pbskids.org

00:26:26.950 --> 00:26:29.120
We'll see you there!
